    "intro_html":  "Carne guisada is the Tex-Mex stew that shows up in a bowl at lunch and in a tortilla at breakfast. Sirloin, tomatoes, jalapeno, and a spoonful of flour that turns the whole thing into its own gravy as it cooks. It thickens up in the fridge, which makes it one of the better containers to open on day four. Each bowl carries \u003cstrong\u003e45 grams of protein\u003c/strong\u003e and 586 calories for about \u003cstrong\u003e$6.33\u003c/strong\u003e (at everyday cost).",
